\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For the spherical fermionic $V_1$ pseudopotential at flux $Q=3(N-1)$, are there $\lambda _*,Delta_*>0$ and $N_*$ such that every real bounded measurable scalar phi with $||\phi ||_infinity\leq 1$ and every $|\lambda |\leq \lambda _*$ gives a unique ground state and spectral gap at least $Delta_*$ for $N\geq N_*$, when lambda times the projected one-body scalar potential is added?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For the spherical fermionic $V_1$ pseudopotential at flux $Q=3(N-1)$, are there $\lambda _*,Delta_*>0$ and $N_*$ such that every real bounded measurable scalar phi with $||\phi ||_infinity\leq 1$ and every $|\lambda |\leq \lambda _*$ gives a unique ground state and spectral gap at least $Delta_*$ for $N\geq N_*$, when lambda times the projected one-body scalar potential is added?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] Original question source or mathematical context.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Uniform-Stability-of-the-Spherical-Laughlin-Gap-October-5-2026/build/sections/01-introduction.tex}.
\item[S2] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
\url{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Uniform-Stability-of-the-Spherical-Laughlin-Gap-October-5-2026/README.md}.
\end{itemize}

